{"title":"","type":"markdown","aggs":[],"params":{"fontSize":12,"openLinksInNewTab":true,"markdown":"## The altitudes of execution, live
Every **unit of work** in the agentic runs Dinis and Angelo make, one document each, from signed sources only (`data/altitude-runs.json`, written by architect.1's `abp/tools/runs-export.mjs`). A run is a tree: **A3** agent → **A2** loops → **A1** LLM calls and **A0** compute; or a **task packet** → each environment's **result** → its calls. Every unit has its own key (`key_fp`), born when it starts and signing its result; `verified` is that signature checked. **Reach** counts capability primitives: needed, held, and **exposure** (held but not needed): above 2 is the *mixing altitudes* finding.

Companion: [Distributed workloads](#/view/d92f4855-670e-f9d4-2337-db284d6856f6) (placements, matrix, Angelo's run log and traces). Fingerprints only, never key material; prompts only as their sha256."}}

{"title":"","type":"markdown","aggs":[],"params":{"fontSize":12,"openLinksInNewTab":true,"markdown":"## A1 calls, from OpenRouter
Every model call the swarm makes through the router (`admin/tools/llm.mjs`) is an **A1 unit** in the altitudes. Here it is from the **provider's side**: OpenRouter sends one OpenTelemetry trace per call to Elastic (Broadcast, `service.name: openrouter`): the model asked and served, the provider that answered, tokens, cost, time to first token and the router's own latency. The same calls are in our ledger and, when they are part of a run, in [The altitudes of execution, live](#/view/b6e128c4-656b-1555-c326-44248b5b62f9).

Prompts and completions are kept in the traces by Dinis's decision, and on **no panel here**: open a trace in Discover to read one."}}
